let's be a little bit better,
let's care about free speech.

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.772
I mean you can see
all those old videos.

00:09:32.772 --> 00:09:34.907 align:start size:88% position:13%
It wasn't like I was
saying anything hateful,

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.776
and yet they were saying all
these horrible things to me,

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:38.277
and people who were
invited to my wedding

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:39.812
were now calling me a Nazi,

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:42.582
and I literally lost
about 40% of my hair,

00:09:42.582 --> 00:09:44.784
and I was spraying
freaking hair on.

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:47.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
People can watch that "Why
I Left the Left" video.

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:49.155
I am bloated and
bags under my eyes.

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:52.558
I looked freaking terrible and
I felt even worse than that.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:56.896
That being said, and this is
partly the purpose of the book,

00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:00.232
I am glad that I
went through it,

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:03.369
I made it to the other side,
and everyone that makes it

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:07.006
to the other side, James
Damore, Bret Weinstein,

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:10.109 align:start size:97% position:3%
Lindsay Shepherd, Ben
Shapiro, the versions of it

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:11.110
that you've gone through.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.745
Everyone that gets through it,

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:14.213
you're stronger
after you did it.

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:17.016
I haven't seen anyone
totally destroyed.

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:19.418 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, that isn't to say people
haven't lost their jobs,

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:21.554
that isn't to say there
aren't people that aren't

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:23.923
public people who have
had all sorts of things,

00:10:23.923 --> 00:10:27.193
but your choice is either
you step up against it

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:30.663 align:start size:84% position:16%
and defend yourself,
so I invited,

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:32.665
what did I do when that New
York Times piece came out?

00:10:32.665 --> 00:10:36.702 align:start position:0%
Literally it had "YouTube's
leading people to the alt right"

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:39.905 align:start size:97% position:3%
with my head was the biggest
head right there above it

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.340
in the New York Times.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
My dad has had a subscription
to the New York Times

00:10:43.643 --> 00:10:46.245
for longer than I'm alive,
something like 45 years.

00:10:46.245 --> 00:10:48.481 align:start position:0%
He had to go to the bagel
place he goes to in Long Island

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:51.317 align:start size:97% position:3%
every Sunday to have a friend
walk up to him and say,

00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:52.818
oh, I didn't know
your son, Dave,

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.620
is a member of the alt right.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.322
Then my dad has to
call me and say,

00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:58.224
what are we talking about here?

00:10:58.224 --> 00:11:00.159
They don't really
affect me anymore

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:01.694 align:start size:81% position:19%
in that I don't
get stress over it

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:04.263
because I think I've come
to know it for what it is.

00:11:04.263 --> 00:11:08.300
It's sort of like
a red pill moment.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:11.404 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's scary at first when
you make that choice,

00:11:11.404 --> 00:11:12.705
but then you get
on the other side

00:11:12.705 --> 00:11:14.440 align:start size:88% position:13%
and when you see
reality for what it is,

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.575 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's like these people
aren't going to destroy me,

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:18.411
they're going to
destroy themselves.

00:11:18.411 --> 00:11:20.846
That's a little bit of what
I want to impart on people.

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:24.417 align:start size:88% position:13%
I want them to know
either you will step up

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.485
and it will suck for a while,

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:29.355
and all sorts of bad
stuff will happen,

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:32.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
but your choice is much
worse, because your choice

00:11:32.324 --> 00:11:34.260
is the frog in the boiling pot.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your choice is to never
live a life that is yours.

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:39.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your choice is to never
say what you really think.

00:11:39.298 --> 00:11:41.934 align:start position:0%
I just refuse to live that way,
and I know you're the same.

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.169
- Here's the thing, though.

00:11:43.169 --> 00:11:45.638 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's easy for us to
say something like this

00:11:45.638 --> 00:11:47.973 align:start size:97% position:3%
because you're married, you're
about to start a family,

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:50.042
you have a successful show.

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.311
I'm kind of happy in my life.

00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:55.047 align:start size:97% position:3%
What do you tell someone who's
like a Nicholas Sandmann?

00:11:55.047 --> 00:11:56.782
What do you tell
these cadets who,

00:11:56.782 --> 00:11:59.151
there's a headline
that says they appear

00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:01.387 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be throwing
white power symbols?

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:03.856
It's really scary
when you're a kid

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:06.492
and now you're in the news,
and people are going to,

00:12:06.492 --> 00:12:10.463
even just joking, be like, hey
Nick, when's the Klan rally?

00:12:10.463 --> 00:12:13.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
You hear that 20 times a day,
it's not gonna feel nice.

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:17.670 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean I don't think
it's easy for us to say,

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
oh, just live your values, but
they don't have that power.

00:12:21.941 --> 00:12:24.677 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well first off, we
should say it's not that

00:12:24.677 --> 00:12:28.347 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's easy for us, it's that
we've been through this thing.

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:31.150
So it's easier for me
now, but it's not like

00:12:32.485 --> 00:12:34.086
it magically was easy.

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:37.289
To your point directly, look,
Sandmann, I've talked to him,

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:38.557 align:start size:81% position:19%
Nick Sandmann, who
everyone knows.

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:40.392
He was the Covington
kid that got slammed

00:12:40.392 --> 00:12:42.294 align:start size:88% position:13%
and slurred by the media
and the whole thing

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.930
and it all turned out
to be a fabrication.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:47.333
I don't know that he's
thrilled that this thing

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:49.969 align:start size:97% position:3%
happened to him, but I know
that as a young person,

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:52.638 align:start size:84% position:16%
he now saw something,
and I think has

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:54.273
a sense of purpose around it.

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:56.475
Another example that I can
give you more specifically

00:12:56.475 --> 00:12:59.478
is Kyle Kashuv, who
used to work with me,

00:12:59.478 --> 00:13:01.747
or he still does work with
us, but now he's in D.C.

00:13:01.747 --> 00:13:04.083
He was one of the
Parkland survivors

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:06.152
who came out as the
gun rights advocate,

00:13:06.152 --> 00:13:08.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
so the media ignored
him at first,

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:09.855
while they made the
rest of them heroes

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.791 align:start size:88% position:13%
because the rest of
them were against guns,

00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:13.058
so they were heroes.

00:13:13.058 --> 00:13:15.461
We find the one kid who
believes in gun rights.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:17.863
We're gonna ignore
him for a while.

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:19.865
Then we don't ignore
him, he's a bad guy.

00:13:19.865 --> 00:13:21.267
Well then, what happened to him?

00:13:21.267 --> 00:13:23.169
It turned out they
found some Google doc

00:13:23.169 --> 00:13:26.305
where he was saying some bad
words with a bunch of friends.

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:28.274 align:start size:84% position:16%
They were just doing
stupid kid stuff

00:13:28.274 --> 00:13:30.476 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you do when you're
15 or 16 years old.

00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:31.744 line:0%
I know Kyle, I love him.

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:34.747 line:0%
There's no way he has a
racist bone in his body,

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:36.816 line:0%
but they tried to destroy
him and what happened?

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:38.984 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Harvard literally
rescinded their offer.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:40.886 line:0%
He graduated number
one in his class.

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:43.489 line:0%
Now I can tell you this.

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:46.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that Kyle is
stronger now than before.

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:49.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now again, these may be
outlier cases, and it sucks.

00:13:49.728 --> 00:13:51.530
I think you're asking
the right question,

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.500 align:start size:88% position:13%
because I'm not denying
that at your job,

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.368
people will look
at you differently.

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:58.838 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean we're not saying
we're real Nazis.

00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:00.739 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're literally saying
if you just have

00:14:00.739 --> 00:14:02.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
some conservative
thought, if you just have

00:14:02.107 --> 00:14:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
some libertarian
thought, if you just say,

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:08.480
oh, I watch Steven Crowder
or I watch Michael Malice,

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.917 align:start size:97% position:3%
that might be enough to have
these people turn on you.

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:15.588
So I'm not saying it's easy,
but I would also say this.

00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:17.690 align:start size:88% position:13%
If you're a young person
going through this,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
especially if you're
a high schooler,

00:14:19.191 --> 00:14:20.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
but if you're a college
person going through this,

00:14:20.626 --> 00:14:25.264 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's not that you should
necessarily come out tomorrow

00:14:25.264 --> 00:14:27.399
and just expect no consequences.

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:29.602 align:start size:88% position:13%
Not only should you
expect the consequences,

00:14:29.602 --> 00:14:31.837
but you can figure out
ways to tease it out

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:34.840 align:start size:97% position:3%
to your friends so that you're
getting stronger over time.

00:14:36.308 --> 00:14:38.043 align:start size:97% position:3%
You don't have to say to
all of your friends at once,

00:14:38.043 --> 00:14:41.146
I've been red pilled, let's
fight about it all day long.

00:14:41.146 --> 00:14:42.982 align:start size:84% position:16%
You might try it with
one friend first,

00:14:42.982 --> 00:14:44.283
test it out, work it.

00:14:44.283 --> 00:14:46.485
Everyone has to do it
with their own rhythm.

00:14:47.786 --> 00:14:49.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's sort of consistent
with the message

00:14:49.221 --> 00:14:51.557 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I put forth in the
book, which is I'm not trying

00:14:51.557 --> 00:14:53.726
to tell everybody what
to do, I'm really not.

00:14:53.726 --> 00:14:55.327
I'm trying to give
you some guidelines

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:58.664
that I think can help get
you through this madness.

00:14:58.664 --> 00:14:59.999
- 11 rules for living.

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:03.068
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:05.604
And the 13th rule is.

00:15:05.604 --> 00:15:08.040
But you know, the truth
is that a lot of this

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:11.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
is sort of Jordan
Peterson-esque in that

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:14.647 align:start position:0%
if you're gonna make a decision
in life to be who you are,

00:15:14.647 --> 00:15:17.316
it's gonna come with some
cost, and you'd better know

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:20.085 align:start size:88% position:13%
how to stand up for
yourself in the process.

00:15:20.085 --> 00:15:22.321
- One of the points
I always harp on

00:15:22.321 --> 00:15:26.592
is that there is a difference
between a bias and an agenda,

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:28.627
meaning we're all gonna
have biases probably,

00:15:28.627 --> 00:15:30.029
news are gonna be slanted.

00:15:30.029 --> 00:15:31.664 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're just simply a
function of our perceptions.

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:34.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
If something feeds into
how we perceive the world,

00:15:34.566 --> 00:15:36.068
humans tend to think it's true.

00:15:36.068 --> 00:15:38.170
If something contradicts,
well I'm gonna have to hear

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.639
some more, because that will
involve a lot of mental work.

00:15:40.639 --> 00:15:44.610 align:start position:0%
One example I use of bias
versus agenda is Stacey Abrams,

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:49.014
who lost the Georgia race
for governor last year

00:15:49.915 --> 00:15:51.116
or the year before.

00:15:51.116 --> 00:15:52.351 align:start size:84% position:16%
She's front and
center all the time,

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:54.053
despite having no
resume to speak of.

00:15:54.053 --> 00:15:57.623
In fact, they decided we're
gonna make this person a star

00:15:57.623 --> 00:16:01.794
regardless of the
inputs of the data.

00:16:01.794 --> 00:16:04.396
Do you think it's more
of a bias over an agenda,

00:16:04.396 --> 00:16:06.398
or am I being too presumptuous?

00:16:07.833 --> 00:16:09.935
- No, I think you're ball
parking it pretty well.

00:16:09.935 --> 00:16:11.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
She's a good example
of this thing

00:16:11.303 --> 00:16:13.372
because she has no resume per se

00:16:13.372 --> 00:16:16.108 align:start size:97% position:3%
other than losing the
Georgia gubernatorial race,

00:16:16.108 --> 00:16:18.877
which she claims she
won, and the media

00:16:18.877 --> 00:16:21.981
and many other progressive
politicians claim she won,

00:16:21.981 --> 00:16:23.549 align:start size:84% position:16%
while at the same time
claiming that Trump

00:16:23.549 --> 00:16:26.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
is the one that doesn't accept
the results of an election,

00:16:26.518 --> 00:16:28.821
of which they are the one
that still don't accept

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:31.690 align:start size:97% position:3%
the results of the
presidential election as well.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:36.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's probably a
little bit of mix of both.

00:16:37.596 --> 00:16:40.366 align:start size:84% position:16%
Again, this is
where once unmasked,

00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:43.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
it just allows them
to destroy themselves.

00:16:44.436 --> 00:16:45.671
There was an article,
you probably saw it

00:16:45.671 --> 00:16:47.406
in Politico in the
last couple of days,

00:16:47.406 --> 00:16:49.708
about Governor Whitmer
in Michigan, who's become

00:16:49.708 --> 00:16:52.678
sort of the face of
the authoritarian
governors right now.

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:54.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
She doesn't want
people planting seeds

00:16:54.213 --> 00:16:55.547
and doing landscaping.

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:58.250 align:start size:88% position:13%
Politico ran a puff
piece on her that said,

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.718
it said something to the effect,

00:16:59.718 --> 00:17:00.986
I'm going to slightly
butcher the words,

00:17:00.986 --> 00:17:02.254
but this will be
pretty damn close

00:17:02.254 --> 00:17:03.889
because I'm not trying
to give fake news here.

00:17:03.889 --> 00:17:07.426 align:start position:0%
It said something to the
effect of you can't find anyone

00:17:07.426 --> 00:17:09.928
in Lansing, Michigan,
who disagrees with her.

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:10.929
- [Michael] That
doesn't like her.

00:17:10.929 --> 00:17:12.297
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:12.297 --> 00:17:13.732
- Yeah, that doesn't like her.

00:17:13.732 --> 00:17:16.168 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's like I'm literally
watching hundreds,

00:17:16.168 --> 00:17:19.505
if not thousands of people
on Twitter who despise her

00:17:19.505 --> 00:17:20.973
who live in her city.

00:17:20.973 --> 00:17:23.675 align:start position:0%
But even if I saw nobody on
Twitter who didn't dislike her,

00:17:23.675 --> 00:17:26.011
the idea that you
can't find anybody.

00:17:26.011 --> 00:17:27.946 align:start size:84% position:16%
Can't do it, there's
literally nobody.

00:17:27.946 --> 00:17:29.782
This woman is Jesus II.

00:17:29.782 --> 00:17:31.016
It's incredible, and by the way,

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:32.217 align:start size:81% position:19%
a lot of people
didn't like Jesus,

00:17:32.217 --> 00:17:33.986
so that wouldn't even
be a good example.

00:17:33.986 --> 00:17:38.323 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's this type of hyperbolic
over the top stuff

00:17:38.323 --> 00:17:40.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
that creates this
perception that, oh,

00:17:40.092 --> 00:17:42.227
you guys lie about this,
you don't tell me the truth

00:17:42.227 --> 00:17:43.695 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it doesn't
fit your narrative,

00:17:43.695 --> 00:17:46.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
so let's just burn the
whole freaking thing down.

00:17:46.031 --> 00:17:47.533 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think this is
where you might be

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:50.069 align:start size:97% position:3%
a little more of a burn
down kind of guy than I am.

00:17:50.069 --> 00:17:53.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is where our tension
is, and I love it.

00:17:53.405 --> 00:17:56.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
I still want to preserve
some of this somehow,

00:17:56.575 --> 00:17:58.644 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you might be right
in the long term,

00:17:58.644 --> 00:18:03.582
that maybe I'm just playing
a slower degradation game.

00:18:03.582 --> 00:18:06.585
I'm worried that if we
just tear it all down

00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:09.955
much faster than it's sort
of organically crumbling,

00:18:09.955 --> 00:18:13.192
that what we get left with
is going to be unthinkable.

00:18:14.326 --> 00:18:16.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You are often
attacked personally.

00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:19.865
You are the poster child
for many of these outlets

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:20.966
and they like to pick on you.

00:18:20.966 --> 00:18:22.201
Ben gets it much worse than you.

00:18:22.201 --> 00:18:23.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean there are
people whose job it is

00:18:23.769 --> 00:18:25.170
just to take whatever Ben says

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:28.440 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and construe it as whatever,
more often than not.

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:31.143 line:0%
Let's name names.

00:18:31.143 --> 00:18:35.347 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Who do you think, what outlet
gets it wrong the most,

00:18:35.347 --> 00:18:36.215 line:0%
in your opinion?

00:18:37.583 --> 00:18:39.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I mean honestly I
don't want to name names,

00:18:39.351 --> 00:18:41.753
not because I'm afraid,
but I don't want to add

00:18:41.753 --> 00:18:42.821
fuel to the fire, because
there are literally people

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:45.257
that watch everything I do

00:18:45.257 --> 00:18:47.926 align:start size:84% position:16%
praying that I will
say their name.

00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:51.396 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's sad, and you know,
the funny thing is

00:18:51.396 --> 00:18:53.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
even as we're talking
here, and I try to do this

00:18:53.866 --> 00:18:55.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we all make mistakes,
but I always try

00:18:55.934 --> 00:18:57.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
to talk about ideas,
not about people.

00:18:57.769 --> 00:19:00.405 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now when I mentioned Governor
Whitmer a second ago,

00:19:00.405 --> 00:19:02.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's like I think that
doesn't include politicians.

00:19:02.975 --> 00:19:05.177 align:start size:97% position:3%
Politicians, I think you sort
of have to go after them.

00:19:05.177 --> 00:19:06.945 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now hopefully you're
going after their ideas.

00:19:06.945 --> 00:19:09.548 align:start position:0%
I didn't attack her personally,
I talked about her ideas.

00:19:09.548 --> 00:19:11.450 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I think politicians,
it's a little bit

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.451
of a different rule.

00:19:13.886 --> 00:19:16.989
There's a certain set of
people that are on YouTube

00:19:16.989 --> 00:19:18.924 align:start size:84% position:16%
or podcast or Twitter
or whatever it is

00:19:18.924 --> 00:19:21.426
that just, I'm good for clicks.

00:19:21.426 --> 00:19:23.629
I left the left and survived.

00:19:23.629 --> 00:19:25.264
They don't want survivors.

00:19:25.264 --> 00:19:26.865
That really is the truth, right?

00:19:28.233 --> 00:19:31.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's easy for them to
attack Ben or attack anyone

00:19:31.503 --> 00:19:33.839
that was a conservative
the whole way through

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:35.307
because it's like you
were supposed to be

00:19:35.307 --> 00:19:36.909
the enemy the whole time.

00:19:36.909 --> 00:19:40.379
But when someone wakes up and
walks, and not just walks,

00:19:40.379 --> 00:19:43.081
but I've succeeded in
the process of that,

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:45.117
I've thrived in the
process of that,

00:19:45.117 --> 00:19:47.853
I've come up with a
cohesive set of views

00:19:47.853 --> 00:19:51.190
and I say what I believe
and people enjoy that,

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's the scariest
thing to them.

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:55.727
So I have no need to
give those guys quarter

00:19:55.727 --> 00:19:58.263
other than that's just a
matter of what the internet

00:19:58.263 --> 00:19:59.765
has sort of become.

00:19:59.765 --> 00:20:02.834 align:start size:97% position:3%
And by the way, it's partly
also why I started locals.com,

00:20:02.834 --> 00:20:04.903
and Michael Malice
has one of the most

00:20:04.903 --> 00:20:06.905 align:start size:84% position:16%
thriving communities
on locals.com,

00:20:06.905 --> 00:20:08.307 align:start size:81% position:19%
and he owns it
and sets the rules

00:20:08.307 --> 00:20:10.275
and can do whatever the
hell he wants there.

00:20:10.275 --> 00:20:14.346
- I'm gonna ask a devil's
advocate question, okay?

00:20:14.346 --> 00:20:17.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
The lowest circle in
hell, according to Dante,

00:20:17.883 --> 00:20:19.651
was for traitors.

00:20:19.651 --> 00:20:22.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think people on
the left should regard you

00:20:22.354 --> 00:20:24.189
as a traitor, and
why or why not?

00:20:25.157 --> 00:20:26.825
- Ooh, I like it, Malice.

00:20:26.825 --> 00:20:28.160
Am I a traitor?

00:20:29.728 --> 00:20:31.163
I'm not a traitor.

00:20:31.163 --> 00:20:35.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, I can't speak exactly
to what their beliefs

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.468
about me are anymore.

00:20:36.468 --> 00:20:38.370
I suppose they would
view me as a traitor.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
They view me as,
you can find videos,

00:20:40.772 --> 00:20:42.307
I was a Bernie supporter.

00:20:42.307 --> 00:20:44.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
The irony is I'm very open
about this whole thing.

00:20:44.343 --> 00:20:47.946 align:start position:0%
You can literally watch me
every week addressing the issues

00:20:47.946 --> 00:20:50.115
and you can watch the movement.

00:20:50.115 --> 00:20:53.652
It wasn't as if one day I was
like, I'm a Bernie supporter.

00:20:53.652 --> 00:20:54.620
- That makes it worse.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:56.455
You're not even hiding it.

00:20:56.455 --> 00:20:59.691
- No, but I'm telling you
that because that shows

00:20:59.691 --> 00:21:01.126
that it's authentic.

00:21:01.126 --> 00:21:03.595 align:start position:0%
You could literally watch
videos, you can find them of me,

00:21:03.595 --> 00:21:06.999 align:start size:97% position:3%
before the 2016 election,
going I'm a Bernie supporter,

00:21:06.999 --> 00:21:09.001 align:start size:84% position:16%
hey liberals, let's
fix this thing,

00:21:09.001 --> 00:21:11.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
what's happening to our
side, all of those things.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.139
Then when that "Why I Left
the Left" video came out,

00:21:14.139 --> 00:21:16.008
the Prager U video,
that was sort of me

00:21:16.008 --> 00:21:17.276
saying good-bye to the left

00:21:17.276 --> 00:21:18.543
and let me see what I
can do with the right,

00:21:18.543 --> 00:21:21.146 align:start size:88% position:13%
and by the way, there's
been great stuff

00:21:21.146 --> 00:21:24.416
happening on the right
for quite some time now,

00:21:24.416 --> 00:21:26.351
and sometimes I think sort
of what you said before.

00:21:26.351 --> 00:21:28.453
Maybe I was wrong about
the right the whole time.

00:21:28.453 --> 00:21:29.721
It doesn't mean the
right's perfect,

00:21:29.721 --> 00:21:31.757
but what you said before
about maybe I was wrong

00:21:31.757 --> 00:21:34.293
about the media the whole
time, maybe I was wrong

00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:37.262
about the right for a
certain period of time.

00:21:37.262 --> 00:21:39.665 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
But that's hard to accept
because it's hard to accept,

00:21:39.665 --> 00:21:41.767 line:0%
oh, the guys that I kept
calling racists and bigots,

00:21:41.767 --> 00:21:43.468 line:0%
they're not racists and bigots.

00:21:43.468 --> 00:21:46.938 line:0%
Maybe I was part of the thing
that was racist and bigoted.

00:21:46.938 --> 00:21:48.407 line:0%
That's a real problem.

00:21:48.407 --> 00:21:50.642 line:0%
Could they think
of me as a traitor?

00:21:50.642 --> 00:21:53.145
Well, I have left
their set of ideas

00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:55.681 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I have openly spoke
about why I did it,

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:59.017 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I have found new
alliances on the other side.

00:21:59.017 --> 00:22:02.487
So if that makes me a traitor,
then I suppose I'm a traitor.

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:05.457 align:start position:0%
- One of the questions I always
yell at with conservatives

00:22:05.457 --> 00:22:08.460
is you guys say that the
media used to be better

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.795
and then it got bad.

00:22:09.795 --> 00:22:12.164
When, in your minds,
was the media better,

00:22:12.164 --> 00:22:13.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
and usually they
don't have an answer.

00:22:13.965 --> 00:22:15.634
You actually gave me
an answer, and this is

00:22:15.634 --> 00:22:18.503 align:start position:0%
the first person I've heard
who actually had a good answer.

00:22:18.503 --> 00:22:20.305
You put it in 1980.

00:22:20.305 --> 00:22:23.075
You put it in 1980
when CNN happened

00:22:23.075 --> 00:22:26.645 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the news happened 24/7,
so now you have to have

00:22:26.645 --> 00:22:29.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
that much more
content, and inevitably

00:22:29.214 --> 00:22:32.751 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's going to lead to
some journalistic standards

00:22:32.751 --> 00:22:35.287
declining, and also if only
because you're competing

00:22:35.287 --> 00:22:38.323
with so many more eyeballs
in a television setting.

00:22:40.225 --> 00:22:43.161
I've always found that
conservatives find CNN

00:22:43.161 --> 00:22:47.532 align:start size:97% position:3%
to be much more agenda driven
and dishonest than MSNBC.

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:48.734
Is that your impression?

00:22:50.168 --> 00:22:52.437
- First off, let's give CNN
some credit for a moment

00:22:52.437 --> 00:22:53.972
because it's not like
you and I do that.

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:55.207
- But you do.

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:56.975 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, I do because
the point is I remember,

00:22:56.975 --> 00:22:59.244
I was in, I think, ninth
grade during the gulf war,

00:22:59.244 --> 00:23:02.314
around '91, and CNN was
on the ground in a war.

00:23:02.314 --> 00:23:03.515
It was incredible to watch.

00:23:03.515 --> 00:23:05.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember being in
school in social studies

00:23:05.484 --> 00:23:07.319 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we would watch clips
and they were doing

00:23:07.319 --> 00:23:10.155
what appeared to be real
journalism and all that,

00:23:10.155 --> 00:23:11.656
so I don't want to
make it seem like

00:23:11.656 --> 00:23:14.326
it was all just horrible all
the time and everything else.

00:23:15.761 --> 00:23:18.663 align:start size:97% position:3%
To your question, I think
the reason people attack CNN

00:23:18.663 --> 00:23:21.900 align:start size:84% position:16%
more than MSNBC, is
that MSNBC leans left,

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
they tell you they're
leaning left, and so be it.

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:27.172 align:start size:88% position:13%
Also they have some
buffoons on the network.

00:23:27.172 --> 00:23:29.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean Al Sharpton was
given a show there.

00:23:29.374 --> 00:23:31.576
Maddow spent two
years running with

00:23:31.576 --> 00:23:35.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Russian collusion hoax
and saw no retribution,

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:38.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
or there was nothing that
happened to her after

00:23:39.518 --> 00:23:41.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
in terms of are we gonna
change our thought processes

00:23:41.753 --> 00:23:44.423
or how we go about
doing these shows?

00:23:44.423 --> 00:23:46.758 align:start size:97% position:3%
CNN was thought of, because
it was the first one,

00:23:46.758 --> 00:23:49.628
it was thought of
as more centrist.

00:23:49.628 --> 00:23:52.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think what's
happened is we all,

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:55.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
regardless of what side
you're on, I think you do,

00:23:55.066 --> 00:23:59.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
even maybe subconsciously,
want centrist news.

00:23:59.004 --> 00:24:01.907
You want something that
feels kind of decent,

00:24:01.907 --> 00:24:04.042
that maybe doesn't
go along with the way

00:24:04.042 --> 00:24:07.512
you think all the time,
and I think that's why

00:24:07.512 --> 00:24:10.015 align:start size:88% position:13%
CNN gets it all the
time, because they went

00:24:10.015 --> 00:24:12.851 align:start size:81% position:19%
from being thought
of as centrist,

00:24:12.851 --> 00:24:14.453
they moved a little
bit to the left,

00:24:14.453 --> 00:24:17.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then the Acosta
thing happened,

00:24:17.189 --> 00:24:20.959
the Brian Stelter thing
happened, the activist,

00:24:20.959 --> 00:24:24.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
let's lie about everybody
and just dismantle

00:24:24.830 --> 00:24:26.431
what journalism is.

00:24:26.431 --> 00:24:28.767 align:start size:88% position:13%
The bigger thing that
I've been thinking about

00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:31.102
and we'll pick this
up in a future show,

00:24:31.102 --> 00:24:32.971
is that a lot of us,
we spend a lot of time

00:24:32.971 --> 00:24:35.106
talking about CNN,
and in a weird way,

00:24:35.106 --> 00:24:37.476 align:start size:84% position:16%
if we all just stopped
talking about CNN,

00:24:37.476 --> 00:24:39.611
almost nobody's watching CNN.

00:24:39.611 --> 00:24:44.616 align:start size:97% position:3%
In a weird way, Trump needs
CNN as the rube in this thing.

00:24:45.484 --> 00:24:47.085
He needs them as the bad guy.

00:24:47.085 --> 00:24:49.421
I'm starting to think
that for the rest of us

00:24:49.421 --> 00:24:52.891
that have broken free, maybe
our next step in breaking free

00:24:52.891 --> 00:24:55.393 align:start size:88% position:13%
is actually really
letting go of that stuff

00:24:55.393 --> 00:24:56.695
instead of reacting to it.

00:24:56.695 --> 00:24:58.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know that
we're quite there yet

00:24:58.129 --> 00:25:00.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it still can
brainwash a lot of people,

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:02.667
but I think that might
be an effective move

00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:05.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
for those of us that have
just moved beyond this thing.

00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:06.638
- Okay, last question.

00:25:06.638 --> 00:25:09.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
Chris Hayes earlier this
week had a monologue

00:25:09.307 --> 00:25:12.010
talking about the Tara Reade
accusations against Joe Biden.

00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:14.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
He went into it at length,
very dispassionately,

00:25:14.846 --> 00:25:17.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying look, it doesn't
matter if you like a person,

00:25:17.949 --> 00:25:20.085 align:start position:0%
if they're prominent, sometimes
these prominent people

00:25:20.085 --> 00:25:21.219
do horrible things.

00:25:21.219 --> 00:25:22.387
You have to look at the evidence

00:25:22.387 --> 00:25:24.322
and throw your emotions aside.

00:25:24.322 --> 00:25:26.458 align:start size:84% position:16%
As a consequence of
this, fire Chris Hayes

00:25:26.458 --> 00:25:27.959
was trending on Twitter.

00:25:27.959 --> 00:25:30.729
So given that his job is
a function of the audience

00:25:30.729 --> 00:25:34.132
and he has bosses that
he has to answer to,

00:25:34.132 --> 00:25:37.702
can't you say, well, it's not
really the fault of the press,

00:25:37.702 --> 00:25:39.604
it's the fault of the population

00:25:39.604 --> 00:25:43.141
that are demanding they be
told what they want to hear?

00:25:43.141 --> 00:25:45.844
- Ah, that's a classic
good Malice question.

00:25:45.844 --> 00:25:47.579
Yes, I think you can.

00:25:47.579 --> 00:25:49.114
We're all doing it to ourselves.

00:25:49.114 --> 00:25:50.549 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's what I always
say about free speech.

00:25:50.549 --> 00:25:52.317 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not worried right
now about the government

00:25:52.317 --> 00:25:53.552
coming for my speech.

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:54.920
I'm not saying I'm
not worried at all,

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:56.421
but that's not my primary worry.

00:25:56.421 --> 00:25:58.723
My primary worry is that we
are doing it to ourselves.

00:25:58.723 --> 00:26:00.659 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
We're actively
silencing ourselves

00:26:00.659 --> 00:26:03.662 line:0%
because we are the ones who
unfurl the mob on each other,

00:26:03.662 --> 00:26:07.332 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and of course inevitably
it will come for you.

00:26:07.332 --> 00:26:09.167 line:0%
As for Chris Hayes,
I would say this.

00:26:10.368 --> 00:26:13.772
He probably just had
his red pill moment,

00:26:13.772 --> 00:26:15.173
and I would say in
a year from now,

00:26:15.173 --> 00:26:16.841
the Chris Hayes you're gonna see

00:26:16.841 --> 00:26:19.978 align:start size:97% position:3%
is gonna be very different,
and probably far more

00:26:19.978 --> 00:26:22.280 align:start size:88% position:13%
like Michael Malice than
like the Chris Hayes

00:26:22.280 --> 00:26:25.450
we know in 2020, because
suddenly he is going to see

00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:28.920 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he said something true,
that we all know is true,

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:32.290
that allegations don't
matter, regardless of

00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:33.925 align:start size:84% position:16%
your political
parties and situation.

00:26:33.925 --> 00:26:36.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
We all know that's the
way it's supposed to work.

00:26:36.161 --> 00:26:39.564
That's all he said, and now
who wants to destroy him?

00:26:39.564 --> 00:26:42.367 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not the conservatives,
it's his own people.

00:26:42.367 --> 00:26:45.170
So if he is able
to survive the mob,

00:26:45.170 --> 00:26:46.771
which is exactly what
this book is about,

00:26:46.771 --> 00:26:49.808 align:start size:88% position:13%
if he's able to do that,
he's on the journey.

00:26:49.808 --> 00:26:52.377
So we should pick it up
in one year from today

00:26:52.377 --> 00:26:53.878
and see where Chris Hayes is.

00:26:53.878 --> 00:26:55.480
A guy who, by the way, has
gone after me many times

00:26:55.480 --> 00:26:57.248
and I don't particularly
like, and I didn't feel

00:26:57.248 --> 00:26:59.951 align:start size:88% position:13%
like offering him any
defense because of that,

00:26:59.951 --> 00:27:01.853 align:start size:88% position:13%
but let's just see
where his journey goes,

00:27:01.853 --> 00:27:04.956
and I suspect we know
where this thing ends.

00:27:04.956 --> 00:27:07.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I've just got one more,
because this just came to me.

00:27:07.392 --> 00:27:10.629
Cenk Uygur, from the Young
Turks, they did this to him.

00:27:10.629 --> 00:27:12.230
He had David Duke on his show,

00:27:12.230 --> 00:27:14.332
which if you had David Duke
on your show, forget it.

00:27:14.332 --> 00:27:16.167 align:start size:84% position:16%
They would bring it
up every five minutes.

00:27:16.167 --> 00:27:19.771 align:start size:97% position:3%
At the end, David Duke says,
"I'm not an antisemite,"

00:27:19.771 --> 00:27:22.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
and Cenk goes, "No,
of course not."

00:27:22.307 --> 00:27:24.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
The New York Times
printed that verbatim,

00:27:24.843 --> 00:27:27.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
as if he said he
wasn't being sarcastic

00:27:27.479 --> 00:27:29.047
and that he took
this at face value.

00:27:29.047 --> 00:27:31.483 align:start size:97% position:3%
Did you follow that story, and
how did that make you feel?

00:27:31.483 --> 00:27:32.917
- I did.

00:27:32.917 --> 00:27:34.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
Listen, I can't believe
you're getting me to do this.

00:27:34.386 --> 00:27:36.054 align:start size:81% position:19%
I will defend Cenk
in that moment

00:27:36.054 --> 00:27:37.756
because he meant
it sarcastically

00:27:37.756 --> 00:27:39.491 align:start size:81% position:19%
from everything
that I could tell.

00:27:39.491 --> 00:27:41.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
He meant it sarcastically
as, oh, of course you're not,

00:27:41.726 --> 00:27:43.561 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the New York
Times ran with it as,

00:27:43.561 --> 00:27:46.231 align:start position:0%
oh, of course you're not,
meaning you're not antisemitic.

00:27:46.231 --> 00:27:50.702 align:start size:88% position:13%
None of this is perfect,
that's the point.

00:27:50.702 --> 00:27:54.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that right there, it's
like the New York Times

00:27:54.773 --> 00:27:58.376
has failed us at
almost every level.

00:27:58.376 --> 00:28:00.512
What I'm enthused
by and what I hope

00:28:00.512 --> 00:28:02.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
this book will bring forth
more than anything else

